  "caveats": {
    "triangle_fold": "Unsupported. No frame in the data shows a triangle fold, so the head can only answer flat, half or quarter. Human fold labels from the labelling workstream (#87) are the path to add it.",
    "label_leakage": "Weak labels: the class equals the check that took the frame (spread, fold1, fold2). The head may learn check-specific camera timing or plate state instead of the fold shape. See sanity_checks: push_off frames show a quarter fold from a check the head never trained on.",
    "no_crepe": "There is no 'no crepe' class. Empty pans (plate_clean frames) come out as quarter with near-certain confidence, so quarter partly means 'little crepe visible'. High confidence is not a presence check: only run the head on frames known to show a crepe (spread and fold checks).",
